tamps` to `ComputeGenerationRawTranscriptTimestamps` and falls back to `ReadGeneration` if raw timestamps not found.\n\n## Review philosophy\n\n- It is OK to find nothing.\n- Be opinionated and consistent.\n- Don't flag trade-offs with no clear winner.\n- High confidence only. Each finding must explain the specific consequence.\n- Don't manufacture findings.\n\n## What to look for\n\n- **Logic errors** — off-by-one, wrong comparison, inverted conditions. Specifically:\n  - In `migrateCheckpointsV2`: `fullCurrentExistsBefore` is computed once, then `packMigratedFullGenerations(..., !fullCurrentExistsBefore)` is called only if `len(migratedFullCheckpoints) > 0`. If migration ran but no checkpoint produced raw transcripts (e.g. all errors or skipped), is `/full/current` ever created? Does that matter for downstream code?\n  - In `migrateOneCheckpoint`: when `existing != nil && !force`, the `errAlreadyMigrated`/`errTranscriptNotGeneratable` error semantics were preserved through a refactor. Trace each path:\n    - `!queuedFullRepair && backfillErr == errAlreadyMigrated` → returns `(nil, errAlreadyMigrated)` → caller marks as **skipped**.\n    - `queuedFullRepair && backfillErr == errAlreadyMigrated` → prints \"queued...\" returns `(fullCheckpoint, nil)` → caller marks as **migrated**.\n    - Both paths are intentional. Confirm or refute by reading the diff.\n  - In `sortMigratableCheckpoints`: stable sort, ties broken by checkpoint ID string. Verify zero-time sentinels go to the END of the list (since `IsZero()` cases return `false` from less, meaning they land after non-zero times). Ensure this is the intended behavior — the comment \"Pack migrated checkpoint generations chronologically\" suggests it.\n  - In `repairOneV2GenerationMetadata`: if `ComputeGenerationRawTranscriptTimestamps` returns `found=false`, the function returns early as \"skipped\". But what if `generation.json` IS stale and there are no raw transcripts (e.g. only main metadata)? Is silently skipping