ce between sub-second and many-seconds.\n>\n> **Trade-offs:** Reverting cleanup to the cheap walker keeps the new repair semantics scoped to repair only, where they belong; cleanup trusts the post-repair `generation.json`.\n>\n> **Evidence:** Cleanup path at `cleanup.go:373`; repair (`generation_repair.go:97`) is the only consumer that genuinely needs the raw recomputation.\n>\n> **Suggested fix:** Cleanup reads `ReadGeneration` first, then falls back to `ComputeGenerationCheckpointTimestamps` only when stored metadata is missing.\n\n> **#3** · Medium · efficiency · `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/generation_repair.go:80-100`\n>\n> **Issue:** `repairOneV2GenerationMetadata` always calls `ComputeGenerationRawTranscriptTimestamps` (full transcript walk) before reading the cheap stored `generation.json`. Order means idempotent re-runs always pay the expensive walk.\n>\n> **Impact if not fixed:** Every `entire migrate` re-run walks all archived generation transcripts even when nothing has drifted. Compounds with #2 because both paths now do the same expensive work.\n>\n> **Trade-offs:** Reading stored `generation.json` first costs one cheap blob read per archived ref; only walk transcripts when stored is missing or invalid (or, alternatively, gate the whole repair pass behind `result.migrated > 0`).\n>\n> **Evidence:** `generation_repair.go:85` (raw walk) precedes `:93` (`ReadGeneration`); `migrate.go:95` runs repair unconditionally.\n>\n> **Suggested fix:** Invert the order — `ReadGeneration` first; recompute from raw only when stored is empty/invalid.\n\n> **#4** · Medium · efficiency · `cmd/entire/cli/migrate.go:183, 212, 380`\n>\n> **Issue:** `migratedFullCheckpoints []migratedFullCheckpoint` accumulates `*checkpoint.SessionContent` (which holds full transcript bytes) for every migrated checkpoint, only partitioning into batches at the end of `migrateCheckpointsV2`. Peak heap ≈ sum of all migrated transcripts.\n>\n> **Impact if not fixed:** On repos with many large historical transcripts, migration peak heap is hundreds of MB, retained until the final pack. Real OOM risk on small CI runners.\n>\n> **Trade-offs:** Streaming each batch (flush whenever buffer reaches `migrateMaxCheckpointsPerGeneration`) caps peak heap at one batch. Slightly trickier error handling, but `pack` already commits per-batch refs, so partial-progress semantics don't change.\n>\n> **Evidence:** Append loop at `migrate.go:212`; partition only at `packMigratedFullGenerations:380`. `migratedFullSession.content` retains transcript bytes.\n>\n> **Suggested fix:** Flush each batch when it reaches `migrateMaxCheckpointsPerGeneration`; drop slice references post-flush.\n\n> **#5** · Medium · test gap · `cmd/entire/cli/migrate.go:222-244` (no test for `sortMigratableCheckpoints`)\n>\n> **Issue:** The new sort has four logical branches (both zero / left zero / right zero / equal / before), but only the `default: left.Before(right)` branch is exercised by `TestMigrateCheckpointsV2_PacksFullGenerationsOldestFirst`.\n>\n> **Impact if not fixed:** A regression in zero-time placement or tie-breaking by checkpoint ID would silently change packing order for migrated repos that have legacy v1 checkpoints with missing `CreatedAt`. Generation membership could shift between archives in confusing ways without test failure.\n>\n> **Trade-offs:** None — pure unit test against a pure function.\n>\n> **Evidence:** Diff of `sortMigratableCheckpoints`; no direct test.\n>\n> **Suggested fix:** Add a unit test covering all-zero, mixed zero+non-zero, equal-non-zero (tie on ID), and a normal mixed case.\n\n> **#6** · Medium · test gap · `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/generation_repair_test.go`\n>\n> **Issue:** Two important no-op paths are unverified: (a) no archived candidates at all → empty result, no push-target resolution; (b) `generation.json` already matches raw-transcript timestamps → `generationMetadataEqual` short-circuit treats the candidate as `Skipped`, not `Repaired`.\n>\n> **Impact if not fixed:** Idempotency regressions in repair (re-running migrate continually rewriting refs and pushing to origin) would not be caught. A bug in `generationMetadataEqual` (e.g. dropping `.Equal` for `==` on `time.Time`) would silently churn refs.\n>\n> **Trade-offs:** None — small additional unit tests.\n>\n> **Evidence:** Only two existing tests, both for the \"stale → repair\" happy path.\n>\n> **Suggested fix:** Add tests for the no-candidates case and the already-correct case.\n\n> **#7** · Low · simplification · `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/generation_repair.go:163-180` vs. `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/cleanup.go:582-600`\n>\n> **Issue:** `pushRepairedV2Generation` and `deleteRemoteRef` build the same `--force-with-lease=<ref>:<oid>` arg, call `remote.PushWithOptions`, and trim/wrap `result.Output` identically. Only the refspec differs.\n>\n> **Impact if not fixed:** Two near-identical 18-line force-with-lease wrappers in the same package; future changes (atomic, retry) must be made twice.\n>\n> **Trade-offs:** A single `pushWithLease(ctx, target, refspec, leaseRef, expectedOID, errCtx string)` helper.\n>\n> **Evidence:** Both helpers shown side by side in the diff.\n>\n> **Suggested fix:** Extract one shared helper; both call sites pass a refspec + lease tuple.\n\n> **#8** · Low · quality · `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/generation_repair.go:90`\n>\n> **Issue:** `repairOneV2GenerationMetadata` returns `(false, nil)` when `ComputeGenerationRawTranscriptTimestamps` finds nothing, while the sibling `addRecomputedGenerationJSON` (`migrate.go:671-684`) falls back to `ComputeGenerationCheckpointTimestamps` for the same condition.\n>\n> **Impact if not fixed:** A latent footgun — an archived ref with only `/main` metadata-derivable timestamps (e.g. partially pruned) would not be repaired even though a correct value can be computed. Today migration always packs raw transcripts so the case is rare.\n>\n> **Trade-offs:** None — call the same fallback chain in both helpers.\n>\n> **Evidence:** `generation_repair.go:89-91` vs. `migrate.go:676-684`.\n>\n> **Suggested fix:** Have `repairOneV2GenerationMetadata` reuse `addRecomputedGenerationJSON`'s fallback chain.\n\n> **#9** · Low · correctness · `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/generation_repair.go:117, 134`\n>\n> **Issue:** The local ref is advanced via `repo.Storer.SetReference` before `pushRepairedV2Generation` runs. Push failure leaves local at the new commit but origin at the old OID; the candidate is reported as `Failed`.\n>\n> **Impact if not fixed:** Transient push failure desyncs local from remote until the next migration run. Self-healing because re-run lists candidates fresh, but the desync window exists.\n>\n> **Trade-offs:** Roll back the local ref on push failure (one extra `SetReference` call).\n>\n> **Evidence:** Order of operations at `generation_repair.go:117` and `:134`.\n>\n> **Suggested fix:** On push failure, restore the local ref to `oldCommitHash` before returning the error.\n\n> **#10** · Low · quality · `cmd/entire/cli/migrate.go:275, 287, 377`\n>\n> **Issue:** `migrateOneCheckpoint` returns three \"shapes\" of `*migratedFullCheckpoint`: `nil` (error), `&migratedFullCheckpoint{}` (no work to pack), and a populated value. The caller checks both `fullCheckpoint != nil` AND `len(fullCheckpoint.sessions) > 0`.\n>\n> **Impact if not fixed:** Cosmetic — both call sites correctly OR-check today. A future caller could forget the second check.\n>\n> **Trade-offs:** None.\n>\n> **Evidence:** Caller at `migrate.go:211`; sentinel returns at `:275, 287, 377`.\n>\n> **Suggested fix:** Return `nil` for the no-work case; collapse caller to a single nil check.\n\n---\n\n**Summary:** 0 Required, 10 Improvements. The branch is merge-ready. The strongest themes are (a) duplication between `ComputeGeneration*Timestamps`, the two force-with-lease push helpers, and the repair-vs-prune fallback chains; (b) efficiency regressions in `entire clean --all` and `entire migrate` re-runs because the raw-t